{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples.md","line":310,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples.tex#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples.tex","label":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","line":699,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[the Hessian of the potential is conformal to $g$]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0145,petersen:page-0146}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f, prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym}\n  \\dcref{ch4:4.3.1}\n  For $f=\\int\\rho\\,dr$ as in \\cref{def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f},\n  $\\mathrm{Hess}\\,f=\\dot\\rho\\,g$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal}\n  \\sketch\n  Since $df=\\rho\\,dr$,\n  \\[\n    \\operatorname{Hess}f=\\dot\\rho\\,dr^2+\\rho\\operatorname{Hess}r.\n  \\]\n  Substitute \\cref{prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym}, namely\n  $\\operatorname{Hess}r=\\dot\\rho\\rho\\,g_H$, to obtain\n  $\\operatorname{Hess}f=\\dot\\rho(dr^2+\\rho^2g_H)=\\dot\\rho\\,g$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[the Hessian of the potential is conformal to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g$\">$g$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368342d686573732d662d636f6e666f726d616c\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0145, petersen:page-0146</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Examples%23def%3Apet-ch4-warping-potential-f\">↗ def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Examples%23prop%3Apet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym\">↗ prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch4:4.3.1</span></span>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f=\\int \\rho \\, dr$\">$f=\\int \\rho \\, dr$</span> as in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Examples%23def%3Apet-ch4-warping-potential-f\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368342d77617270696e672d706f74656e7469616c2d66\">subsection 3.1</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathrm{Hess}\\, f=\\dot\\rho \\, g$\">$\\mathrm{Hess}\\, f=\\dot\\rho \\, g$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Examples%23prop%3Apet-ch4-hess-f-conformal\">↗ prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal</a> \\sketch Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df=\\rho \\, dr$\">$df=\\rho \\, dr$</span>, </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\operatorname {Hess}f=\\dot\\rho \\, dr^2+\\rho \\operatorname {Hess}r.  \\]\">\\[  \\operatorname {Hess}f=\\dot\\rho \\, dr^2+\\rho \\operatorname {Hess}r.  \\]</span></p><p> Substitute <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh04_Examples%23prop%3Apet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368342d686573732d722d726f7473796d\">subsection 2.3</a>, namely <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Hess}r=\\dot\\rho \\rho \\, g_H$\">$\\operatorname {Hess}r=\\dot\\rho \\rho \\, g_H$</span>, to obtain <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {Hess}f=\\dot\\rho (dr^2+\\rho ^2g_H)=\\dot\\rho \\, g$\">$\\operatorname {Hess}f=\\dot\\rho (dr^2+\\rho ^2g_H)=\\dot\\rho \\, g$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#rem:pet-ch4-warped-product-canonical-form","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f","title":"def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f","label":"def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym","label":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","label":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","label":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#rem:pet-ch4-warped-product-canonical-form","title":"rem:pet-ch4-warped-product-canonical-form","label":"rem:pet-ch4-warped-product-canonical-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#ex:pet-ch4-hess-f-space-forms","title":"ex:pet-ch4-hess-f-space-forms","label":"ex:pet-ch4-hess-f-space-forms"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[the Hessian of the potential is conformal to $g$]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0145,petersen:page-0146}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f, prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym}\n  \\dcref{ch4:4.3.1}\n  For $f=\\int\\rho\\,dr$ as in \\cref{def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f},\n  $\\mathrm{Hess}\\,f=\\dot\\rho\\,g$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch4-hess-f-conformal}\n  \\sketch\n  Since $df=\\rho\\,dr$,\n  \\[\n    \\operatorname{Hess}f=\\dot\\rho\\,dr^2+\\rho\\operatorname{Hess}r.\n  \\]\n  Substitute \\cref{prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym}, namely\n  $\\operatorname{Hess}r=\\dot\\rho\\rho\\,g_H$, to obtain\n  $\\operatorname{Hess}f=\\dot\\rho(dr^2+\\rho^2g_H)=\\dot\\rho\\,g$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f","title":"def:pet-ch4-warping-potential-f","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch04_Examples#prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym","title":"prop:pet-ch4-hess-r-rotsym","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}